    <tr>
      <td width="582" valign="top" height="0" bgcolor="#808000">
      <span style="mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;MS Mincho&quot;"><b><i><font color="#FFFFFF">Note
for the High level Hunters:<o:p>
      &nbsp;</font></i></b>
</span>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td width="582" valign="top" height="0">
<p class="MsoPlainText"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;MS Mincho&quot;">In
the past, my only hope for getting a high end item was to buy it. To do this I
had to sell everything I could get my hands on.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp;
</span>Now we are becoming capable of looting these things for ourselves.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp;
</span>One thing I would like to get going as a guild policy is the trickle down
factor.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Especially when a very cool
item is looted during a guild hunt. This may mean the item does not really
belong to the person, but to the guild.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>When
the person using it gets something better.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp;
</span>It goes to the next member in line that has most need of the item.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp;
</span>This would only go for items looted on guild hunts, and very high level
stuff at that.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Things like Shiny
Metallic Robes and Ykesha Swords or Thick Banded Belts.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp;
</span>Not your average Fine Steel weapon or such.<o:p>
</o:p>
</span></p>
<p class="MsoPlainText"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;MS Mincho&quot;">One
thing that will be needed to be taken into account is Skills.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span>For a month I put everything I could get into Fletching.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp;
</span>It cost me close to 3000 plat to get there but I'm maxed at 200.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp;
</span>Now I sell bows to the members<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>for
cost. Currently Ladielilacs Jewelry Skill is 177.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp;
</span>She can make some great stuff and she too sells what she makes to guild
members at COST.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Absorbing the cost
of failures herself.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>She is working
hard on getting those last points so she can make Platinum Jewelry for us.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp;
</span>She does and must sell everything she can.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp;
</span>And I give her as much as I can also.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp;
</span>But its incredibly expensive. So our money goes there.<o:p>
</o:p>
</span></p>
<p class="MsoPlainText"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;MS Mincho&quot;">&nbsp;<o:p>
</o:p>
</span></p>
<p class="MsoPlainText"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;MS Mincho&quot;">I
just don't want people to think that we tell people to share, but we don't do it
ourselves.<o:p>
</o:p>
</span></p>
<p class="MsoPlainText"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;MS Mincho&quot;">&nbsp;<o:p>
</o:p>
</span></p>
